## Biographies
Juan Ding Xiao received her Ph.D. in 2017 from the University of Science and Technology of China (USTC), supervised by Prof. Hai-Long Jiang. She has subsequently worked at the Institute of Nuclear Energy Safety Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS). Her research interest is the synthesis and photocatalysis of MOF-based materials.
Hai-Long Jiang earned his Ph.D. in 2008 from Fujian Institute of Research on the Structure of Matter, CAS. He subsequently worked at the National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology in Japan, first as an AIST Fellow and later as a JSPS Fellow during 2008−2011. After a postdoctoral stint at Texas A&M University in the U.S., he became a full professor at USTC in 2013. He is a Fellow of the Royal Society of Chemistry (FRSC) and was recognized as a highly cited researcher (2017 and 2018) in chemistry by Clarivate Analytics. His research interest currently lies in crystalline porous and nanostructured materials for energy/environment-related catalysis.
